<block><txt break.before="1">An Act to apply laws of the State, other than
criminal laws, to the coastal sea adjacent to the State.</txt></block></tier>
</content>


<content type="body">

<level type="clause" id="sec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e1cc054c-31d9-4c0d-9a82-02016f427dc7"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>1</no><heading guid="_56dff4fc-051c-4384-878d-0e4ab0e20988"
id="sec.1-he"><b>Name of Act</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act may be cited as the <legref
refid="act-1980-146" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Application of Laws (Coastal Sea) Act
1980</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_2eae616f-80ca-414a-8d4c-e89880e2000f"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>2</no><heading guid="_ce8dc0ac-e021-4aba-bfcb-d4b90201b2f8"
id="sec.2-he"><b>Commencement</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.2-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_68e640c6-3f73-4405-a198-e86652dddb50"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This section and section 1 shall commence on the
date of assent to this Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.2-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f8070167-d6f2-4d4e-82eb-d21e60f40f7b"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Except as provided by subsection (1), this Act
shall commence on such day as may be appointed by the Governor in respect
thereof and as may be notified by proclamation published in the
Gazette.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_09352827-2788-49f1-b0ef-ec6168330adf"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>3</no><heading guid="_0f795b75-c6d8-46e4-bb7c-dc53f4aa0048"
id="sec.3-he"><b>Definitions</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c7a58c55-2590-4948-9202-fbf4fa125d82"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act, except in so far as the context or
subject-matter otherwise indicates or requires:</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_04d49164-5aae-4244-8030-6b165071691c"
id="sec.3-def.coastalsea"><b><i>coastal sea</i></b></defterm> means:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_10c47a2e-e2b0-4e55-92c1-47ae9b2bc0a8" id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the territorial sea adjacent to the State,
and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_1e58b7da-62ef-451e-9d87-ccb876e88075" id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the sea on the landward side of the territorial
sea adjacent to the State that is not within the limits of the
State,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">and includes the airspace over and the seabed and
sub-soil beneath any such sea.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_ff495603-26b9-471e-8333-cb25ed4f698c"
id="sec.3-def.criminallaws"><b><i>criminal laws</i></b></defterm> means the
substantive criminal law, and the law of criminal investigation, procedure and
evidence, within the meaning of the <legref refid="act-1998-173" jurisd="NSW"
type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Crimes at Sea Act
1998</i></name></legref>.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_e116ae0d-1f42-40b8-8079-8fee39bea5fd"
id="sec.3-def.territorialsea"><b><i>territorial sea</i></b></defterm> means
the territorial sea of Australia.</txt></block></deflist>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_589e5e17-1ad3-495d-a0ca-91d4af84dc54"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act, a reference to a law in force in the
State includes a reference to the provisions of any instrument made under that
law.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_78654fb0-5c2f-4be2-ac11-d788309d6098"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act, a reference to the laws in force in
the State does not include a reference to any law to the extent to which it
would, if it were to apply by virtue of this Act, regulate or purport to
regulate coastal trading, as mentioned in section 736 of the <legref
jurisd="IMP" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Merchant
Shipping Act 1894</i></name></legref> of the Imperial
Parliament.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 3:</b> Am 1998 No 173,
Sch 2.1.</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_28b9e4db-a15a-4b7d-9cde-e3d81f496ac6"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_3b0251c5-e21d-4a9d-aa80-e201060dd716"
id="sec.4-he"><b>Application of laws to coastal sea</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The provisions of the laws in force in the State,
whether written or unwritten, and whether substantive or procedural, and as in
force from time to time, other than criminal laws and laws of the
Commonwealth, apply to and in relation to the coastal sea, and so apply as if
the coastal sea were part of the State.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_60b93fa2-7852-4382-ba61-a5b1de6b23d1"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_b36b4d92-13ff-4483-a108-40c380a4459e"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Laws with specific application not to
apply</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_8dd82503-3dad-4ab4-9e3e-819ceee63869"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Nothing in this Act renders a provision of the
laws in force in the State applicable to a particular place:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_422276e1-f651-40f2-94e3-e57923dfaf31" id="sec.5-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">in so far as the provision is incapable of
applying to or in relation to that place,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_a5e39c9b-51ba-465d-987e-3f3b9e0f82af" id="sec.5-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">if those laws expressly provide that the
provision does not extend or apply to or in relation to that place,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_5fdb7394-d618-4eab-b783-410d74817bda" id="sec.5-ssec.1-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">if those laws expressly provide that the
provision applies only in a specified locality in the State that does not
include that place.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_9f324327-c565-4456-b07e-b233309f031b"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A provision of the laws in force in the State
shall not be taken to be a provision to which subsection (1) applies by reason
only that it is limited in its application to acts, matters and things within
the territorial jurisdiction of the State or within the territorial or
adjacent waters (however described) of the State.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_0a580f98-6171-4a44-a5a7-540a7e471050"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_9e5f5ef9-247c-487d-a2c1-54459b9c18fc"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Extent of jurisdiction in relation to coastal
sea</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_20c8397f-198d-43bf-ba15-89af8d7ee443"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">All persons who may exercise powers and
authorities conferred on them by law for the purposes of or in connection with
a provision of any law in force in the State shall have and may exercise all
or any of those powers and authorities for the purposes of or in connection
with that provision as applying by virtue of this Act, as if the coastal sea
were part of the State.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b8d04577-d9f3-4672-92c6-c957f774309c"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The several courts of the State are invested with
jurisdiction in all matters arising under the provisions of the laws as
applying by virtue of this Act, as if the coastal sea were part of the
State.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a43e1639-88bc-4f10-adcb-315a09350f1f"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_d3cc185d-4b6e-40fc-940e-a0dff0a21b62"
id="sec.7-he"><b>Regulations</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7c0422d5-a03f-4bcc-9636-5ce7d4b42018"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may make regulations, not
inconsistent with this Act, for or with respect to prescribing all matters
required or permitted by this Act to be prescribed or necessary or convenient
to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to this
Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_5a00ccef-b310-43f1-ad10-c34e471fe337"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Without limiting the generality of subsection
(1), the regulations may provide that such provisions or classes of provisions
of the laws in force in the State as are specified in the regulations:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_038a97a5-7130-4d55-aeb8-4abdaf2e4cea" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">do not apply by virtue of this
Act,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_2c5b42b3-b81e-4c3b-8aa4-f6e5c9906fd9" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">do not apply by virtue of this Act to acts,
matters or things, or classes of acts, matters or things, specified in the
regulations, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_aa43fccf-7066-47fc-8316-0c219aade715" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">do not apply by virtue of this Act in
circumstances specified in the regulations.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1b7bb6ba-e23b-4a9d-930d-823e08231b19"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Where regulations such as are referred to in
subsection (2) are in force, this Act shall be construed to apply the
provisions of the laws in force in the State subject to and in accordance with
the regulations.</txt></block></tier>
</level>
</content>


